greetings anime fans i've been looking  at the feedback from a previous video  and it looks like i learned a little  something you guys can't get enough of  anime final fights the 500k view says  something about it so i'm here to  deliver more without further ado here  are my next favorite final fights in  anime after going through some of the  most epic final fights in anime before  what else does the medium have in store  let's find out let's start with shiro vs  gilgamesh  if you were to rank my favorite fate  series battles this must be near the top  for me unlimited blade works is the  perfect sequel to fate zero in terms of  narrative and while each route has its  pros i feel that this is the route that  leads to the most natural conclusion of  the story that started in zero after all  this is the route where shiro comes to  understand his ideals and uses his  knowledge to cleanly beat the king of  heroes it's an underdog battle which  doesn't even feel like one thanks to  shiro perfectly countering gilgamesh's  abilities he made our hero look like a  badass worth a million bucks with how he  gets under gilgamesh's skin it's a  complete trouncing of gilgamesh that  feels deserved and well-earned it also  has my favorite remix of the emiya theme  so that's something as well  let's move on to an underrated fight  shinichi versus goto  when i first watched parasite i already  knew that it's not your ordinary anime i  was fully dazzled by the themes and the  narrative that the show carried and i  especially enjoyed the dynamic between  shinichi and migi i'd be lying if i said  that i didn't get emotional when  shinichi lost migi towards the end but  that makes the triumph in the final  battle against gotoh so special left  without his trusted buddy for once  chinichi had to go deep into his bag of  tricks to fend off this ultimate  parasite the reunion was emotional but  the finishing blow well that felt even  more satisfying technically speaking  parasite's final conflict is against  someone else in a brilliant thematic  twist however in terms of boss fights  this is it and it's one of the best  anime final fights that we have  [Music]  next i put kira versus josuke on the  list  how can we have a final fight video  without a mention of jojo especially  this epic showdown that we have here  just gate finally gets his hands on gira  after so long and their fated showdown  left everyone wanting more it's got a  lot of stakes riding on it this one it  has the usual jojo goodness of wacky out  of this world abilities for a show where  you'd expect a lot of craziness to  happen jojo does have its share of well  animated and hype inducing instances of  cqc this is just one of many examples of  sakuga in the series but i feel that  this moment is the best embodiment of it  manga readers have commented on how the  fight could have been handled better but  i think in the grand scheme of things  it's fine anime owners love this  showdown and it's a great way to wrap up  the saga  the same can be said of castlevania as a  series but this last fight pretty much  gives the series a send-off to remember  honestly i'm as much as a gamer as i am  an anime fan and this battle just gives  that big boss vibe it manages to  recapture the thrill of playing a game  and coming face to face with the  ultimate enemy those godlike beings that  you so often see in jrpgs trevor shows  no fear as he faces death himself in  this epic finale and i've got to give a  lot of props to the banter it's not too  often you'd see trash talking this  badass do you it's got some cool action  and a wild ending so make sure to stay  tuned with some amazing animation and  art i was more hyped than ever watching  this fight it felt so good rekindling  the fire that i had for video games back  in my childhood  spike versus vicious from cowboy bebop  is a banger that i failed to include the  last time around rewatching it i  concluded that it's not just my  nostalgia goggles working the fight's  legitimately what you'd love and expect  from a setting like cowboy bebop this is  one of those high-stakes frantic paced  final battles built for hollywood  thrillers and cowboy bebop is one of the  anime fights like this are made for  shootouts sword fights hand-to-hand  combat this fight has got it all this  battle caps off an epic journey with one  of the most gut-wrenching endings you  can have this one's a keeper and if you  need something to convince your  non-anime fan friends what anime can be  like and you can definitely show them  this fight  let's move on with another classic anime  now shall we yomi versus yusuke is one  of the battles that stuck with me  the yomi fight is something that i find  memorable because of a simple fact  yusuke loses where else do you see that  in shonen anime back when i was much  younger and watching yuyu hakusho i  didn't think that it was possible for  the protagonist to lose a high stakes  final battle but he did and having it  happen relatively early in the  tournament it completely blew my mind  away yuyu hakusho continues its string  of breathtaking tournament arc with the  three kings arc you get your fair share  of magical attacks but i think that the  emotional weight of the clash is what  sold me on it despite finding a new  power like most protagonists do use gate  still doesn't have what it takes to beat  yomi leaving more than a few fans  disappointed at least he didn't go down  without putting on an entertaining show  though did he it all worked out in the  end and you can't tell me that this  fight doesn't have its share of  emotional moments that had us hooked for  minutes on end  i'm not sure how hot of a take this is  but i feel that dragon ball z should  have ended in the cell saga it's the  most organic ending for the series with  a real touching passing of the torch  moment from goku to gohan but you know  executive meddling and money means that  the show must go on a lot of people talk  about it like it's a bad thing which at  times it really is however without said  executive meddling we would have gotten  some awesome moments to be fondly  remembered like a lot of the nifty  fights in dragon ball super a decade ago  have you wondered what dragon ball would  look like with modern colors and  technology super's got you covered that  or this final battle against kid buu by  all means i don't think it's the best  dragon ball z fight out there but it's  got all you want in a finale an  over-the-top battle full of run-ins and  everyone contributing in their own ways  to finally bringing down kid buu i just  love these all your powers combined  final attacks that they often do in  anime and the super spirit bomb is one  of my first encounters with the trope  [Music]  let's continue with the oldie but goody  train with vash versus knives  brother battles are cool because often  they already carry that emotional weight  required for us to care about the fight  more than that there's just something  appealing about good old one-on-one  shootouts trigun's final battle does  just that and leaves me very satisfied  the fight does an excellent job of  giving us a sense of tension with each  move and the action has little dead air  as you can feel each brother's will to  defeat the other it also has that crazy  quick draw scene that culminates in a  breathtaking sequence well for its time  where vash steals victory from the jaws  of defeat the fight's just so smooth and  fluid for its time as well and when i  don't think it's aged too well it was  spectacular when i first saw it  speaking of brother battles how about a  look at hyakimaru vs tahomaru  for me much of donaro's appeal is the  chase besides the budding relationship  with doraro the adventure of following  hikimaru in his quest to get his body  parts one by one is the thing that  thoroughly immersed me in the series  that's why this final battle feels like  such a good payoff yakimaru vs tahomaru  is every bit as intense as you'd expect  from the climactic battle of an  action-adventure story and it delivered  the fight choreography is top notch and  the momentum shifts throughout the  battle kept me on the edge eagerly  awaiting for the next phase of the  battle besides this great fight i also  like the message and the catharsis  factor in this fight yakimaru deciding  to spare his brother is such a strong  moment considering what happened  beforehand it's a very powerful ending  to a long and treacherous journey and it  made every step on the way worth it  [Music]  so which is your favorite fight amongst  these i want to know your thoughts so  make sure to check out the comments and  do a bit of sharing it helps youtube  algorithm and i'd love to talk to you  guys about your favorite final fights  too if you're interested you can also  check out our channel memberships for  perks also don't forget to drop by  patreon your support would really be  appreciated that does it for today thank  you for watching and hope to see you  again  [Music]
 

